tsf|n|The hair that grows on the chin, lips, and adjacent parts of the human face, chiefly of male adults. ; The long hairs about the face in animals, as in the goat. ; The cluster of small feathers at the base of the beak in some birds ; The appendages to the jaw in some Cetacea, and to the mouth or jaws of some fishes. ; The byssus of certain shellfish, as the muscle. ; The gills of some bivalves, as the oyster. ; In insects, the hairs of the labial palpi of moths and butterflies. ; Long or stiff hairs on a plant; the awn; as, the beard of grain. ; A barb or sharp point of an arrow or other instrument, projecting backward to prevent the head from being easily drawn out. ; That part of the under side of a horse's lower jaw which is above the chin, and bears the curb of a bridle. ; That part of a type which is between the shoulder of the shank and the face. ; An imposition; a trick.	a:7jsj,158,13;4h05,151,1;1686,130,20;8dee,111,3;a2ux,97,1;ml8,96,8;90ka,94,2;5dvi,83,2;5l7w,76,37;7tbo,67,1;35om,64,32;aj94,62,144;3udu,61,20;8nwv,60,7;4dw4,60,5~aj94,62,144;5dsp,27,58;3ifa,31,48;5l7w,76,37;7t8z,37,32;35om,64,32;ys5,36,29;wyo,24,21;3udu,61,20;1686,130,20;8mqp,21,16;6tfq,7,14;7jsj,158,13;3uj8,31,11;53yv,12,11	v:8lfb,93,9;8y9l,84,5;8lf2,74,5;zqz,71,1;9uqg,66,6;12ty,61,1;3d0z,40,3;3voq,40,5;35om,34,4;3vog,26,3;789p,21,5;4y61,8,2;1bsr,5,2~8lfb,93,9;9uqg,66,6;8lf2,74,5;789p,21,5;3voq,40,5;8y9l,84,5;35om,34,4;3d0z,40,3;3vog,26,3;4y61,8,2;1bsr,5,2;12ty,61,1;zqz,71,1	V:8lf3,113,29;3dva,105,2;47mm,69,12;2ngu,69,4;9uqg,63,5;3xs4,60,2;3vpa,57,13;3usu,56,5;9uqq,54,2;ah94,50,6;3vog,45,11;3voq,43,6;8q9u,42,7;7ji3,25,2;562e,16,3~8lf3,113,29;3vpa,57,13;47mm,69,12;3vog,45,11;8q9u,42,7;8arb,1,6;ah94,50,6;3voq,43,6;9uqg,63,5;3usu,56,5;1olc,3,5;2ngu,69,4;562e,16,3;3xs4,60,2;9uqq,54,2	n:3s9k,120,2;8dee,95,1;zqz,91,4;90ka,84,1;2mv8,64,19;689d,62,8;9lju,62,5;3usz,54,11;41zh,53,4;9mxs,50,3;78fi,49,1;8nwv,42,2;4t8m,38,2;aj94,28,14;2gyg,26,2~2mv8,64,19;asmk,15,17;aj94,28,14;3usz,54,11;689d,62,8;9